# Experiment: Implementation of Docker Commands & Containerization Using Docker

## Aim

To learn and implement basic Docker commands and perform containerization of an application using Docker.

---

# Objective

* Install Docker.
* Understand basic Docker commands.
* Create and run Docker containers.
* Build a Docker image.
* Containerize a simple application.

---

# Prerequisites

* Docker Desktop installed
* Git Bash / Command Prompt
* Internet Connection

---

# Step 1: Verify Docker Installation

Open Git Bash or Command Prompt:

```bash
docker --version
```

Expected Output:

```bash
Docker version 28.x.x
```

---

# Step 2: Check Docker Information

```bash
docker info
```

Displays Docker system information.

---

# Step 3: Check Running Containers

```bash
docker ps
```

Output:

```bash
CONTAINER ID   IMAGE   COMMAND   STATUS
```

---

# Step 4: Check All Containers

```bash
docker ps -a
```

Displays running and stopped containers.

---

# Step 5: Download Docker Image

Pull Ubuntu image:

```bash
docker pull ubuntu
```

Verify:

```bash
docker images
```

Output:

```bash
REPOSITORY   TAG      IMAGE ID
ubuntu       latest   xxxxx
```

---

# Step 6: Run Docker Container

```bash
docker run -it ubuntu
```

You will enter the Ubuntu container shell.

Check Linux version:

```bash
uname -a
```

Exit container:

```bash
exit
```

---

# Step 7: Start Existing Container

```bash
docker start <container_id>
```

Example:

```bash
docker start a1b2c3d4
```

---

# Step 8: Stop Container

```bash
docker stop <container_id>
```

Example:

```bash
docker stop a1b2c3d4
```

---

# Step 9: Remove Container

```bash
docker rm <container_id>
```

Example:

```bash
docker rm a1b2c3d4
```

---

# Step 10: Remove Docker Image

```bash
docker rmi ubuntu
```

---

# Step 11: Create a Simple Application

Create a file named:

```text
index.html
```

Content:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Docker Demo</title>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Hello Docker Container</h1>
</body>
</html>
```

---

# Step 12: Create Dockerfile

Create file:

```text
Dockerfile
```

Content:

```dockerfile
FROM nginx:latest

COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
```

---

# Step 13: Build Docker Image

Navigate to project folder:

```bash
cd DockerDemo
```

Build image:

```bash
docker build -t docker-demo .
```

Verify:

```bash
docker images
```

---

# Step 14: Run Container from Image

```bash
docker run -d -p 8080:80 docker-demo
```

Where:

* `-d` → Detached mode
* `-p` → Port mapping

Check container:

```bash
docker ps
```

---

# Step 15: Access Application

Open browser:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

Output:

```text
Hello Docker Container
```

---

# Step 16: View Container Logs

```bash
docker logs <container_id>
```

Example:

```bash
docker logs a1b2c3d4
```

---

# Step 17: Execute Commands Inside Container

```bash
docker exec -it <container_id> bash
```

Example:

```bash
docker exec -it a1b2c3d4 bash
```

---

# Common Docker Commands

| Command            | Description          |
| ------------------ | -------------------- |
| docker --version   | Check Docker version |
| docker images      | List images          |
| docker ps          | Running containers   |
| docker ps -a       | All containers       |
| docker pull ubuntu | Download image       |
| docker run         | Create container     |
| docker stop        | Stop container       |
| docker start       | Start container      |
| docker rm          | Delete container     |
| docker rmi         | Delete image         |
| docker build       | Build image          |
| docker logs        | View logs            |
| docker exec        | Access container     |

---

# Architecture

```text
Application Files
       |
       v
   Dockerfile
       |
       v
 Docker Image
       |
       v
 Docker Container
       |
       v
 Application Running
```

---

# Output

* Docker installed successfully.
* Docker commands executed successfully.
* Docker image created.
* Container launched successfully.
* Application deployed inside Docker container.

---

# Result

Thus, the implementation of Docker commands and containerization using Docker was performed successfully. A Docker image was created from the application, and the application was executed inside a Docker container.
